* AWS Autoscaling 
>> Autoscaling is region specific
>> Autoscaling is evenly disturbed.
>> Creating group of EC2 instance that can scale up or down depedning on condition you set. 
Note : Scale out -- increasing server, scale in -- decreasing server
>> Enable elasticity by scaling horizontially through adding or terminating EC2 instance. 
>> Autoscaling ensure that you have right number of EC2 instances for your needs at all the time. 
NOte : Cost effective and no extra cost for the instance launch via autoscaling. 
      : Autoscaling enable your serivces to be fault tolerance and elastic. 
	 
* Auto scaling components 
>> Lauch configuration -- like instance type , AMI , keypair security group
>> Autoscaling group -- Group name , group size , vpc , subnet , health check period
>> Scaling policy -- Metric type , Target volume 

* Autoscaling balancing 
>> If autoscaling find that number of EC2 instance launched by ASG into subjet AZ are not evenly disturbed and ASG will re autoscaling by itself. 
>> AS always try to balance the instance disturbed across AZ. 
>> While rebalancing , ASG launch new instance EC2 where are the less number instance then terminates instance where no. of instance are more. 

What caused inbalance of EC2 instance 
>> If we add or remove subnet or avaialbity group from autoscaling group.
>> If you requesting EC2 termination from autoscaling group. 
>> An AZ doens't have enough EC2 capacity now has enough capacity and it is one of the autoscaling group. 

----> We can attach a running EC2 instance to  an autoscaling group by using AWS console or CLI  if the condition are met. 
>> Instance must be an running state. 
>> AMI used to launch the EC2 instance still exist. 
>> Instance is not part of another autoscaling group. 
>>  Instance is in the same AZ of the same  group. 
>> If the existing EC2 instance under the autoscaling group, plus the one to be needed, exceed the max capacity of autoscaling group, the request will fail, EC2 instance would not be added.
 
>> You can manually remove EC2 instance from autoscaling group using AWS consle or CLI. 
>> You can manage the deattach instance independently  or attach to another autoscaling group. 
>> When you detach an instance , you have option to reduce the autoscaling group capacity.
>> When you delete autoscaling group it's parameter like max, min and desired capacity are all set to zero, hence it terminates all EC2 instance. 
>> If you wan to keep EC2 instance and manage then independently then detach then first from autoscaling group before deleting autoscaling group. 

** Elastic load balancer with with autoscaling group
>> We can add one or more elastic load balancer to our autoscaling group.
>> Elastic load balancer must be in same region as of autoscaling group. 
>> Once , you do this , any EC2 instance existing or added by the autoscaling group will be automatically defined at elastic load balancer.
>> You do not need to register those instance manually on the autoscaling group defined elastic load balancer
>> Instance and the ELB must be in the same VPC. 

** EC instance health check in autoscaling
>> Autoscaling classifies it's EC2 instance health status either healty  or unhealth. 
>> By default , AS uses EC2 status check only to determing health status of an instance. 
>> When you have once or more ELB defined with the autoscaling group, you can configure autoscaling to use both EC2 health check and ELB health check to  determine instance health. 
>> Health check peroid is 300 sec by default. 
>> If we set zero , in grace period ,  the instance health is checked once it is in service. 
>> Untill the grace period  timer expires any unhealthy status reported by EC2 status check, or the ELB attached to the autoscaling group will not be acted upon. 

---> When grace peroid expire the autoscaling group would consider an instance unhealthy as follows 
>> EC2 status check report to autoscaling group instance state other then  running. 
>> If ELB health check configured used by autoscaling group reported instance as out of serivce.
>> Unlike AZ rebalancing , termination of unhealthy instance happen first, then autoscaling attempt to launch new instance to replace ones terminated. 
>> Elastic IP and EBS volume get detched from terminated instance you need to manually attach them to the new instance. 

