**Standby state
>>  You can manually move an instance from an ASG and put it in standby state. 
>> Instance in standby state are still managed by autoscaling. 
>> Instance in standby state are chargeable. 
>> Standby instance are not count towards available resources. 
>> health check up is not done during standby state. 


** Autoscaling policies 
>> It is of two type -- Manual/static and Dynamic 
>> Dynamic policies -- Target tracking , Simple scaling policy and step scaling  policy
     -- Target tracking -- keep the load to a particular limit.for eg cpu ultilization 70%
	 -- Simple scaling policy -- it set the limit of load , if increase above that then add particular server defined at time of policy creation. 
	 -- Step scaling policy -- here load are managed via step scaling set at it creation. It doesn't support cool down period. 


** Scaling policies 
>>  Define how much you want to scale based on defined conditions. 
>> Autoscaling group uses alarms and policies to determine scaling. 
>>  For Simple or step scaling , a scaling ajdustment cna't change the capacity of the group above the max group size or below the group size. 
>> Predective scaling : It will check history of the Autoscaling group load and manage the load efficiently . or you can also schudulded the number of instance. It uses machine learing to predict pattern. 
>> Traget tracking policies : Manage  the load to a particular limit.for eg cpu ultilization 70%
>> Simple scaling policy -- it set the limit of load , if increase above that then add particular server defined at time of policy creation. 
>> Step scaling policy -- here load are managed via step scaling set at it creation. It doesn't support cool down period. 

